	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105040828142?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The project 'FinFinder' is based on an Fish species recognition system target towards improving the identification of species and their representation by rounding off the rough edges of Machine Learning, specifically Convolution and Region-based Convolutional Neural Networks. It is a comprehensive system capable of recognizing the species of fish captured with images through web resources or special cameras, allowing for the differentiation of even the most similar species of fish. FinFinder allows such features as provision for fish quality testing and recommend recipes depending on the nature of the investigated species's market price and connecting to external market via APIs to other external websites. The system is also an economic web application, where fish can be bought and sold without having to change applications. It is designed overload the population that does not consist of fishery specialists. The development of fish species recognition system and realisation of its distinct features has significantly widened the scope of services offered for planning and animal husbandry. The paper highlights the process of development, the implementation of the system and the prospects for its implementation in aquaculture and culinary art. © 2026 IEEE.}
